ADDENDA <Act No. 8352, Apr. 11, 2007>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation; provided, the amended provisions of subparagraph 1b of Article 2, subparagraph 7 of Article 2, Articles 8(2)2, 35(1)1, and 36(1)1, and Article 15(28), (35), and (66) of Addenda shall enter into force on July 4, 2007.
Article 2 (Transitional measures concerning enforcement date)
As prescribed by proviso to Article 1 of Addenda, until the amended provisions of subparagraph 1b of Article 2, subparagraph 7 of Article 2, Articles 8(2)2, 35(1)1 and 36(1)1 enter into force, the former subparagraph 1b of Article 2, subparagraph 9 of Article 2, Articles 8(2)2, 37(1)1 and 38(1)1 equivalent to the amended provisions shall apply.
Article 3 (Transitional measures concerning site of facilities necessary for agricultural production)
The previous provisions shall apply to a site of the facilities necessary for agricultural production under subparagraph 1b of Article 2 installed with the permission for farmland conversion under the previous Farmland Preservation and Utilization Act and the Farmland Expansion and Development Promotion Act or with the report on farmland conversion under the previous Act on the Special Measures for Development of Agricultural and Fishing Villages at the time of January 1, 1996, the date the Farmland Act, Act No. 4817 enters into force.
Article 4 (Transitional measures concerning existing owners of farmland)
(1) Articles 6(1), 10, 11, 23 and 62 shall not apply to the ownership of the farmland with respect to a person who owned the farmland at the time of January 1, 1996, the date the Farmland Act, Act No. 4817 enters into force. However, Article 43-3 of the former Act on the Special Measures for Development of Agricultural and Fishing Villages shall apply to the period for disposition and the purchase in consultation, etc. with respect to the farmland subject to the disposition, of which disposition has not been made by a person who is to dispose of under Article 43-2(2) of the former Act on the Special Measures for development of Agricultural and Fishing Villages.
(2) A person who owned the farmland exceeding the maximum limit of farmland ownership under Article 7 at the time of January 1, 1996, the date the Farmland Act, Act No. 4817 enters into force, may continue to own the farmland concerned notwithstanding the provisions of the same Article.
Article 5 (Transitional measures concerning designation of agricultural promotion area)
The agricultural promotion area designated under the former Act on the Special Measures for Development of Agricultural and Fishing Villages at the time when this Act enters into force shall be deemed to have been designated under this Act.
Article 6 (Transitional measures concerning permission for farmland conversion)
(1) A person who has obtained permission for farmland conversion and a person who filed the report on farmland conversion under the previous Farmland Preservation and Utilization Act, the Act on the Special Measures for Development of Agricultural and Fishing Villages and the Farmland Expansion and Development Promotion Act at the time of January 1, 1996, the date the Farmland Act, Act No. 4817 enters into force, shall be deemed to have obtained the permission for farmland conversion or the permission on temporary use of farmland for another purpose or to have made the report on farmland conversion under this Act.
(2) The farmland which was passed through the consultation concerning the farmland conversion or on which the consent or the approval was obtained concerning the farmland conversion under the former Farmland Preservation and Utilization Act at the time of January 1, 1996, the date the Farmland Act, Act No. 4817 enters into force, shall be deemed to have been passed through consultation concerning the farmland conversion under this Act.
(3) The farmland located in the area designated as the residential area, the commercial area and the industrial area under Article 17(1) of the Urban Planning Act and the farmland not passed through the consultation concerning the farmland conversion under the former Farmland Preservation and Utilization Act as the farmland determined to be the proposed site for the urban planning facilities at the time of January 1, 1996, the date the Farmland Act (Act No. 4817) enters into force, shall be deemed to have been passed through consultation concerning the farmland conversion under Article 34(2)1 of this Act.
Article 7 (Transitional measures concerning farmland creation costs)
(1) A person who has paid the cost required to create farmland under Article 4(4) of the former Farmland Preservation and Utilization Act or the amount required for the new development of farmland under Article 53(3) of the former Farmland Expansion and Development Promotion Act at the time of January 1, 1996, the date the Farmland Act, Act No. 4817 enters into force, shall be deemed to have paid the farmland preservation charges under this Act.
(2) A person who was notified to pay the cost required to create farmland under Article 4(4) of the former Farmland Preservation and Utilization Act or the amount required for the new development of farmland under Article 53(3) of the former Farmland Expansion and Development Promotion Act at the time of January 1, 1996, the date the Farmland Act, Act No. 4817 enters into force, shall be deemed to have been notified to pay the farmland preservation charges under this Act.
(3) An amount per unit classified by farmland of the farmland creation cost determined and publicly notified under Article 4(5) of the former Farmland Preservation and Utilization Act at the time of January 1, 1996, the date the Farmland Act, Act No. 4817 enters into force, shall be deemed to have been determined and publicly notified under this Act.
(4) Where the farmland located in the area designated as the residential area, the commercial area and the industrial area through the consultation made before July 29, 1981 under Article 4(2) of the Farmland Preservation and Utilization Act is converted to another use after January 1, 1996, the date the Farmland Act, Act No. 4817 enters into force, Article 38(1)2 shall not be applicable to this.
Article 8 (Transitional measures concerning certificate of farmland purchase and sale)
Any person who was issued the certificate of farmland purchase and sale under Article 19(2) of the former Farmland Reform Act and under Article 19 of the former Farmland Lend-Lease Management Act at the time of January 1, 1996, the date the Farmland Act, Act No. 4817 enters into force, shall be deemed to have been issued the qualification certificate for acquisition of farmland under in this Act.
Article 9 (Transitional measures concerning farmland ledger)
The farmland ledger under Article 14 of the former Farmland Preservation and Utilization Act at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed as the farmland ledger under this Act.
Article 10 (Transitional measures according to restriction on division of farmland)
The amended provisions of Article 22(2) shall not apply to the division of farmland for which application was made or of the case where authorization and permission accompanying the division of farmland under the relevant statutes or regulations was applied at the time of January 1, 2003, the date the amended Act of the Farmland Act, Act No. 6793 entered into force.
Article 11 (Transitional measures concerning restriction on conduct in agricultural protection area)
The former provisions shall apply to the restriction on conduct of a person who has obtained the authorization, permission, approval, etc. or made the report and applied for the authorization, permission, approval, etc. under the provisions of the relevant statutes or regulations concerning the installation of a building, a structure and other facilities restricted under the amended provisions of Article 32(2) in the agricultural protection area at the time of January 22, 2006, the date the amended Act of the Farmland Act, Act No. 7604 entered into force.
Article 12 (Transitional measures concerning production facilities of agricultural and stock farm products in definition of farmland)
Notwithstanding subparagraph 1b of Article 2 and subparagraph 7 of that Article, the previous provisions shall apply to a site for production facilities of agricultural and stock farm products for which permission for farmland conversion was obtained or on which the report on farmland conversion was accepted under the previous provisions of at the time of July 4, 2007, the date the amended Act of the Farmland Act, Act No. 8179 enters into force.
Article 13 (General transitional measures concerning disposition)
The conduct of an administrative agency or the conduct to an administrative agency under the former provisions at the time when this Act enters into force shall be deemed as the conduct of an administrative agency or the conduct to an administrative agency under this Act equivalent to the former provisions.
Article 14 (Transitional measures concerning penal provisions)
When the penal provisions apply to the conduct prior to the date this Act enters into force, the former provisions shall apply.
Article 15 Omitted.
Article 16 (Relation with other statutes or regulations)
Where the former Farmland Act or the provisions thereof have been cited by other statutes or regulations at the time when this Act enters into force, if the provisions equivalent to those provisions cited are in this Act, this Act or the equivalent provisions shall be deemed to have been cited in place of the previous provisions.

